{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi5P7fvjF9xPn8Wq3GmJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EKX8tWSajUHjZL85FMJQVV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"grep -n \"E.shade\\b\\|^- \\`E.shade\\|rig.hand(\" engine/API-INDEX.md | head -5; grep -n \"^- \\`game.setZoom\\|^- \\`r.actor({ outline\\|outline:\" engine/API-INDEX.md | head -5","description":"Check shade, hand and outline signatures"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19912,"cache_read_input_tokens":380727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19912},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e21ad4c-7b98-4203-a651-095d6be0bc50","uuid":"2c107637-bc5e-4d95-829a-b6d19d8d1b5a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:51:53.927Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi5P7N4yxmcVAWUaB2bx","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EKX8tWSajUHjZL85FMJQVV":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-072345__xcf3323/work/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-072345 && grep -n \"E.shade\\b\\|^- \\`E.shade\\|rig.hand(\" engine/API-INDEX.md | head -5; grep -n \"^- \\`game.setZoom\\|^- \\`r.actor({ outline\\|outline:\" engine/API-INDEX.md | head -5","description":"Check shade, hand and outline signatures"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01EKX8tWSajUHjZL85FMJQVV":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-072345__xcf3323/work/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-072345"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EKX8tWSajUHjZL85FMJQVV","type":"tool_result","content":"181:- `E.shade(h, a)`: shade('#336699', -0.3) darker, (+0.3) lighter. Hue-shifted like painted pixel art: darker drifts cool, lighter drifts warm\n671:- `rig.hand(which = 'R')`: world position of a hand ('R' holds the weapon): spawn bullets, sparks or thrown things here\n355:- `E.font`: Pixel fonts. 'normal' (default) is a 5x7 proportional font with lower case; 'tiny' is the 3x5 upper-case font. text(g, str, x, y, color, opts) where opts is an outline color, false, or { font: 'normal' | 'tiny', outline: '#0b0814' | false, shadow: '#000' (1 px drop shadow), gradient: ['#fff', '#8ad'] (top to bottom), scale: 1, align: 'left' | 'center' | 'right', wrap: maxWidthPx, lineGap } '\\n' starts a new line. Returns { w, h } of the drawn block. title(...) draws big logo text.\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are drawn by code, so they re-rasterize crisply at the new size; HUD text and overlays stay the same.\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e21ad4c-7b98-4203-a651-095d6be0bc50","uuid":"191f4950-c36b-4719-a6fb-0e026d6ae630","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:51:53.960Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"181:- `E.shade(h, a)`: shade('#336699', -0.3) darker, (+0.3) lighter. Hue-shifted like painted pixel art: darker drifts cool, lighter drifts warm\n671:- `rig.hand(which = 'R')`: world position of a hand ('R' holds the weapon): spawn bullets, sparks or thrown things here\n355:- `E.font`: Pixel fonts. 'normal' (default) is a 5x7 proportional font with lower case; 'tiny' is the 3x5 upper-case font. text(g, str, x, y, color, opts) where opts is an outline color, false, or { font: 'normal' | 'tiny', outline: '#0b0814' | false, shadow: '#000' (1 px drop shadow), gradient: ['#fff', '#8ad'] (top to bottom), scale: 1, align: 'left' | 'center' | 'right', wrap: maxWidthPx, lineGap } '\\n' starts a new line. Returns { w, h } of the drawn block. title(...) draws big logo text.\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are drawn by code, so they re-rasterize crisply at the new size; HUD text and overlays stay the same.\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EKX8tWSajUHjZL85FMJQVV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
