{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi8yqozx5KqtP2m1gVmx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrapping up: writing the engine-change notes, then the final exit interview, rebuild and full test pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":681576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e21ad4c-7b98-4203-a651-095d6be0bc50","uuid":"2c98bb6c-d83a-450c-a98f-5af3baedec9e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:38:56.539Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi8yqSRj3sMqSdHrVf5N"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi8yqozx5KqtP2m1gVmx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019MwYq6MdPfdDs7x4nCU7Jn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff copy)\n\nEach change is marked `// EF:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`.\n\n1. **Dialog voices that babble** (`Dialog.update`). `talk.voice` may now be a function: it is called once for every newly\n   revealed letter with `(char, index, pageText)`, instead of a preset blip on every second letter. The game's\n   `EF.babble.voiceFor(speaker)` returns such a function (Animalese-style formant syllables). Why: the commentary, the\n   story and the PA need per-letter gibberish voices with pitch contours, and the stock voice could only play an SFX.\n2. **Kit patterns and shirt numbers** (`Humanoid` torso painter). A rig option `kit: { pattern: 'hoops' | 'stripes' |\n   'halves' | 'sash' | 'plain', color2, number, numberColor }` paints bands clipped to the torso plate after the base fill,\n   and the shirt number (tiny font) on the back when the rig faces away from the camera. Why: football kits are the\n   clubs' identity; plain shirts with trim could not show Kipperton's hoops or Opulence's stripes.\n\nNot changed (done in game code instead, using engine internals): the crowd and voice audio buses connect to\n`game.audio._master` and use `game.audio._noise` (the plan's `audio.bus()` idea); goal nets collide in game code instead\nof TileMap walls (walls render as solid blocks); the PlayStation glyph default is a game setting that replaces the\nstandard `glyphs` setting (no engine change needed).\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the engine changes document"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":681576,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881},"output_tokens":57,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e21ad4c-7b98-4203-a651-095d6be0bc50","uuid":"3092cedb-bc25-4bfd-9dcf-99badbcbb34d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:39:03.113Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi8yqSRj3sMqSdHrVf5N","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019MwYq6MdPfdDs7x4nCU7Jn":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-072345__xcf3323/work/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-072345 && cat > engine/CHANGES-ENGINE.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff copy)\n\nEach change is marked `// EF:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`.\n\n1. **Dialog voices that babble** (`Dialog.update`). `talk.voice` may now be a function: it is called once for every newly\n   revealed letter with `(char, index, pageText)`, instead of a preset blip on every second letter. The game's\n   `EF.babble.voiceFor(speaker)` returns such a function (Animalese-style formant syllables). Why: the commentary, the\n   story and the PA need per-letter gibberish voices with pitch contours, and the stock voice could only play an SFX.\n2. **Kit patterns and shirt numbers** (`Humanoid` torso painter). A rig option `kit: { pattern: 'hoops' | 'stripes' |\n   'halves' | 'sash' | 'plain', color2, number, numberColor }` paints bands clipped to the torso plate after the base fill,\n   and the shirt number (tiny font) on the back when the rig faces away from the camera. Why: football kits are the\n   clubs' identity; plain shirts with trim could not show Kipperton's hoops or Opulence's stripes.\n\nNot changed (done in game code instead, using engine internals): the crowd and voice audio buses connect to\n`game.audio._master` and use `game.audio._noise` (the plan's `audio.bus()` idea); goal nets collide in game code instead\nof TileMap walls (walls render as solid blocks); the PlayStation glyph default is a game setting that replaces the\nstandard `glyphs` setting (no engine change needed).\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the engine changes document"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_019MwYq6MdPfdDs7x4nCU7Jn":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-072345__xcf3323/work/EurophoriaFootball-EuropeanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-072345"}}}
